**1. A system for reading a multi-cell microfluidic plate, the system comprising:**  

a multi-cell microfluidic plate comprising a plurality of cells, each cell including:  
a loading well configured to receive a fluid sample;  
a central through hole extending through the plate;  
a spiral microfluidic channel disposed about the central through hole and in fluid communication with the loading well; and  
an outlet hole in fluid communication with a terminal end of the spiral microfluidic channel;  

a plate holder configured to position the multi-cell microfluidic plate;  

an illumination source configured to direct excitation light toward at least a portion of the spiral microfluidic channel of each cell;  

an optical detector configured to detect an optical signal from the fluid sample within the spiral microfluidic channel; and  

a processor configured to associate the detected optical signal with a respective cell and determine, based on the detected optical signal, a characteristic of the fluid sample in the respective cell.
